<title>BRAZIL: Vicunha wins Brazil Bahia/Sergipe Band B bidding.</title>
<headline>Vicunha wins Brazil Bahia/Sergipe Band B bidding.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Vicunha consortium won the concession to run B Band cellular services in the northeast Brazilian states of Bahia and Sergipe, official said.</p>
<p>Officials from the Ministry of Communications said Vicunha, of Brazilian concern Vicunha, the investment wing of the Globo media group, private bank Bradesco and Italy's Stet, offered 250 million reais for the service, just 20 million reais above the government's minimum price.  </p>
<p>Only three groups bid for the Bahia/Sergipe service area.</p>
<p>Earlier, the Communications Ministry awarded the metropolitan Sao Paulo cellular Band B concession to a group including U.S. operator BellSouth Corp.</p>
<p>((-- William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom 55-61-3141183))</p>
